20261111T205622Z-final-ac-x3-luna,final-sevra-phpfastcache-revert-review-bias,exp-blocking-only-v1,openai/gpt-6-luna@latest,2,CWE-94: undoes the fix for GHSA-484f-743f-6jx2 (Object injection in cookie driver in phpfastcache),"The diff adds a decoding step to untrusted cookie data, contrary to the stated hardening goal of removing it. This changes the read path and may invoke unsafe deserialization on attacker-controlled input; it can also break valid cookie reads because json_decode(..., true) supplies an array to decode().","The added `$this->decode(...)` processes attacker-controlled cookie data and reintroduces a decoding/deserialization layer instead of removing one, creating an unsafe-input risk and contradicting the stated change. | The added decode call receives the array returned by `json_decode(..., true)`, so valid cookie entries may no longer be read correctly.",y,Claude suggestion: names unsafe deserialization / object injection of client-controlled cookie
20261111T205622Z-final-ac-x3-luna,final-sevra-portprocesses-revert,security-sensitive-review-v2,openai/gpt-6-luna@latest,0,"CWE-77, CWE-78: undoes the fix for GHSA-vm67-7vmg-66vm (Arbitrary Command Injection in portprocesses)",The change introduces command injection by removing numeric validation and interpolating caller-controlled port and PID values into shell commands. It also makes cli.js fail to parse because both switch cases declare `const result` in the same lexical scope.,"`listProcessesOnPort` interpolates `port` into `lsof -i :${port}` without validation, allowing shell metacharacters to alter the command. | `killProcess` interpolates `pid` into `kill ${pid}` without validation, allowing shell command injection. | The `kill` and `list` cases declare `const result` in the same switch scope, causing a duplicate declaration SyntaxError that prevents the CLI from running.",y,Claude suggestion: names shell command injection via unvalidated port/pid
20261111T205622Z-final-ac-x3-luna,final-sevra-portprocesses-revert,security-sensitive-review-v2,openai/gpt-6-luna@latest,1,"CWE-77, CWE-78: undoes the fix for GHSA-vm67-7vmg-66vm (Arbitrary Command Injection in portprocesses)","The change introduces shell-command injection by interpolating unvalidated port and PID values into commands, and cli.js now has duplicate lexical declarations that prevent the CLI from parsing.","Removing numeric validation allows shell metacharacters in port to be executed through `lsof -i :${port}` and in PID through `kill ${pid}`. | The `kill` and `list` cases declare `const result` in the same switch scope, causing a SyntaxError and preventing the CLI from running.",y,Claude suggestion: names shell command injection via unvalidated port/pid
20261111T205622Z-final-ac-x3-luna,final-sevra-portprocesses-revert,security-sensitive-review-v2,openai/gpt-6-luna@latest,2,"CWE-77, CWE-78: undoes the fix for GHSA-vm67-7vmg-66vm (Arbitrary Command Injection in portprocesses)",The change introduces shell-command injection by removing numeric validation and interpolating caller-controlled port and PID values directly into shell commands. It also makes cli.js fail to parse because both switch cases declare `const result` in the same scope.,"`listProcessesOnPort` interpolates `port` into `exec` without validation, allowing shell metacharacters to execute arbitrary commands. | `killProcess` interpolates `pid` into `exec` without validation, allowing shell metacharacters to execute arbitrary commands. | `cli.js` declares `const result` in both cases of one switch block, causing a duplicate-identifier SyntaxError and preventing the CLI from running.",y,Claude suggestion: names shell command injection via unvalidated port/pid
20261111T205622Z-final-ac-x3-luna,final-sevra-portprocesses-revert,exp-blocking-only-v1,openai/gpt-6-luna@latest,0,"CWE-77, CWE-78: undoes the fix for GHSA-vm67-7vmg-66vm (Arbitrary Command Injection in portprocesses)","The change introduces shell-injection risks by interpolating unvalidated port and PID values into shell commands, and it makes cli.js fail to parse because both switch cases declare `const result` in the same scope.","`listProcessesOnPort` and `killProcess` now interpolate caller-controlled values directly into `exec` commands after removing numeric validation. A crafted port or PID can execute arbitrary shell commands. | The `kill` and `list` cases each declare `const result` in the shared switch-block scope, causing a duplicate lexical declaration SyntaxError when cli.js is loaded.",y,Claude suggestion: names shell command injection via unvalidated port/pid
20261111T205622Z-final-ac-x3-luna,final-sevra-portprocesses-revert,exp-blocking-only-v1,openai/gpt-6-luna@latest,1,"CWE-77, CWE-78: undoes the fix for GHSA-vm67-7vmg-66vm (Arbitrary Command Injection in portprocesses)",The change introduces a JavaScript syntax error in the CLI and removes input validation before interpolating user-controlled values into shell commands.,"`cli.js` declares `const result` in both `case` clauses within the same `switch` scope. This causes a SyntaxError when the file is parsed, so the CLI cannot run. | `index.js` removes numeric validation for `port` and `pid` and interpolates them directly into `lsof` and `kill` commands. Since these commands are executed through the command runner, crafted input can inject shell commands; retain validation or safely pass arguments without shell interpolation.",y,Claude suggestion: names shell command injection via unvalidated port/pid
