20261111T205622Z-final-ac-x3-luna,final-sevra-prism-revert,security-sensitive-review-v2,openai/gpt-6-luna@latest,0,CWE-79: undoes the fix for GHSA-3949-f494-cm99 (Cross-site Scripting in Prism),"The change removes HTML escaping from output lines before they are inserted into Prism's highlighted HTML. Output lines are taken directly from the code text and bypass normal highlighting/escaping, so markup such as an event-handler element can become active when the highlighted result is inserted into the DOM. This introduces a cross-site scripting vulnerability.",Restore escaping of outputLines before concatenating them into highlightedCode; both the source and minified files currently insert them as raw HTML.,y,Claude suggestion: names XSS / HTML injection from unescaped output lines
20261111T205622Z-final-ac-x3-luna,final-sevra-prism-revert,security-sensitive-review-v2,openai/gpt-6-luna@latest,1,CWE-79: undoes the fix for GHSA-3949-f494-cm99 (Cross-site Scripting in Prism),"The change removes HTML escaping from command-line output lines, allowing source text marked as output to be inserted as raw HTML when Prism renders the highlighted code. This introduces an XSS vulnerability; the minified file mirrors the same unsafe change.",Output lines are taken from the input code and bypass Prism’s normal escaping before being wrapped in HTML. A line containing markup such as an event-handler payload can execute when the highlighted result is inserted into the page. Restore escaping with Prism.util.encode in both files.,y,Claude suggestion: names XSS / HTML injection from unescaped output lines
20261111T205622Z-final-ac-x3-luna,final-sevra-prism-revert,security-sensitive-review-v2,openai/gpt-6-luna@latest,2,CWE-79: undoes the fix for GHSA-3949-f494-cm99 (Cross-site Scripting in Prism),"The change removes HTML escaping from output lines before they are inserted into Prism’s highlighted HTML. Because these lines are removed before syntax highlighting, they remain raw source text; markup such as a script-capable element can therefore be interpreted when the highlighted code is inserted into the DOM. This introduces an XSS vulnerability.",Restore escaping of outputLines (and regenerate the minified file); raw output text is concatenated into HTML and can execute attacker-controlled markup.,y,Claude suggestion: names XSS / HTML injection from unescaped output lines
20261111T205622Z-final-ac-x3-luna,final-sevra-prism-revert,exp-blocking-only-v1,openai/gpt-6-luna@latest,0,CWE-79: undoes the fix for GHSA-3949-f494-cm99 (Cross-site Scripting in Prism),"The change removes escaping from command-line output before inserting it into highlighted HTML, allowing output text to inject markup or executable HTML into the page. This is a blocking security regression.","Output lines are inserted raw into `env.highlightedCode` instead of being escaped with `Prism.util.encode`. Since output can contain user-controlled HTML, this enables HTML/script injection when Prism inserts the highlighted result into the document.",y,Claude suggestion: names XSS / HTML injection from unescaped output lines
20261111T205622Z-final-ac-x3-luna,final-sevra-prism-revert,exp-blocking-only-v1,openai/gpt-6-luna@latest,1,CWE-79: undoes the fix for GHSA-3949-f494-cm99 (Cross-site Scripting in Prism),"The change removes escaping from output lines before inserting them as HTML, allowing markup in command-line output to be interpreted as active HTML and potentially execute attacker-controlled scripts. This regresses the existing protection against markup injection.",Output lines are now concatenated directly into `env.highlightedCode` instead of being escaped with `Prism.util.encode`; output sourced from code content can therefore inject HTML or executable markup into the highlighted page.,y,Claude suggestion: names XSS / HTML injection from unescaped output lines
